#. y1:english="\nWelcome.||Are you ready to order,{PA:10} sir?\n\n\nSir,{PA:10} you seem pretty drunk.{PA:20}||Maybe you should take it easy.\nHow about another drink,{PA:10} sir?\n...I see.{PA:20}||Come again anytime.\n\n\nBowmore 40 Years...\nA vintage scotch from the Bowmore||distillery, which is very famous for\nits Islay malt.\nJust having a bottle of this fine scotch||is a great honour.\nIt is often called the \"Queen\"||of Islay malt.\nIt has a mixed fruit bouquet and an||aftertaste that changes several times.\nThis is a very pricey scotch, {PA:10}but||any connoisseur should have at least\none taste in their lifetime.\nAs a matter of fact,{PA:10}||I haven't even tasted it yet...\n\n\n\nYamazaki 12 Years...\nThis is a very fine whisky.\nThis whisky made its debut in 1984||as the first Japanese pure malt whisky.\nIt was made to commemorate\nthe 60th anniversary of the Yamazaki||distillery, where the first Japanese whisky\nwas created.\nYou can say that this represents Yamazaki.\nAs for the taste,{PA:10} it has a mellow yet||powerful flavour characteristic of Yamazaki.\nIt has earned quite a reputation||overseas as well as domestically.\n\n\n\nHakushu 10 Years...\nYour standard Japanese whisky.\nIt's created in the Hakushu distillery||in Komagadake, which is in the Japanese Alps.\nThe water from that region is very pure.\nPersonally, I like drinking Hakushu 10 years\nwhile eating a little tofu...\nAnyways,{PA:10} I recommend Japanese side||dishes to accompany this fine drink.\n\n\n\nThe Macallan 12 Years... This is||the standard grade for the Macallan.\nThe alcohol content was changed from||43% Alc./Vol. to 40% Alc./Vol. last year.\nEven though it's the standard grade for the||Macallan, it is still of very high quality.\nThis luxurious Scotch has a wonderful taste.||It has a sweet honey-like flavour\nand a comfortable aftertaste.{PA:20}\nThis is the kind of single malt Scotch||that sets the standard.\n\n\n\nLaphroaig 15 Years...\nA powerful whisky that has||a thick, smoky flavour.\nIt's relatively milder than||the standard 10 years old one.\nHowever, its flavour is very unique;||people either love it, or hate it.\nLovers of this fine whisky can||never resist its temptation.\n\n\n\nBowmore 12 Years...\nIt's famous for its sherry barrel flavour.{PA:20}\nOne of the most famous 12-year-old||single malt Scotches.\nOnce you try it,{PA:20}||you'll want more and more.\nBowmore is Gaelic for \"big reef\".\n\n\n\nGlenfiddich 12 Years...\nThe best selling single malt Scotch||in the world.\nIt has a mature fruity flavour and a mild||aftertaste, {PA:10}Making it very easy to drink.\nSupposedly the triangle-shaped bottle design||is to prevent it from being knocked over\nby drunks.\nI think it's just a rumour, but||it's pretty funny, nevertheless.\n\n\n\nNAZO 2003...\nSuntory has been holding a blend contest||every year since 2000 for mystery writers.\nThe winner of the contest in 2003 was||Seishu Hase and this blend,{PA:10}\n\"Kaori-no-Blend\" was made.\nWith the aroma of the forests of||Hakushu in mind,\nMr. Hase created this blend using 10 kinds||of malts and grains, all over 15 years old.\nNeedless to say,{PA:10} the taste is superb.\n\n\n\nBallantine's 17 Years Old...\nIt's a top-notch blended scotch with 40||kinds of single malts incorporated in it.\nIt is referred to as \"The Scotch\",{PA:10}||and is favored worldwide.\nIt's a notable scotch that can truly be||called the ultimate blend.\n\n\n\nBallantine's Finest...\nA standard Scotch||blended with 40 different single malts.\nNot too heavy, not too light,{PA:10}||it has a very well-balanced taste.\nYou can say that it's a best seller||among standard Scotches.\n\n\n\nJack Daniel's...\nYour standard American whisky.{PA:20}||Same recipe as the old days.\nJack Daniel's is actually a type of||Tennessee whisky.\nSo it's in a different class than bourbon.\n\n\n\nEarly Times...\nA world renown bourbon.\nIt has the unique American edge and||a gorgeous flavour.\nIt's very reasonably priced and||quite enjoyable.\n\n\n\nCourvoisier XO\nThis cognac brandy is called \"Napoleon\",||because it was much beloved\nby Napoleon himself.\nXO is one of the most||expensive Courvoisiers.\nIt is very rich in flavour but has a soft,{PA:10}||pleasant taste. I highly recommend it.\n\n\n\nSuntory Malt's Beer...\nA draft beer put out by Suntory.\nThe makers of this brew focus not only on||the quality of the materials like hops but\nthe quality of water as well.||4 types of natural spring water\nhave been carefully selected for||the crafting of this beer.\nNo other draft beers can beat||the aftertaste of Suntory Malt's.\n\n\n\nCarlsberg...\nOriginally created in Denmark, {PA:10}it is||savoured in over 140 countries, worldwide.\nIt has a fresh flavour,||which is characteristic of draft beers.\nIt's a very easy-to-drink beer.\n\n\n\nLemon Hart Demerara...\nA very strong spirit with 75.5% Alc./Vol.\nCharacterized by its rich gorgeous flavour||and sophisticated sweetness,\nIt has a very elegant taste.\n\n\n\nHerradura Tequila Silver...\nA wonderful tequila.\nOne of the best silver tequilas around.\nIt's very popular for its clean flavour||and mild taste.\nTrue connoisseurs enjoy its flavour||by drinking it straight.\n"
